    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Y5ejC4NegC7mwSGKCtTw6k)_\n\n## Problem\nInserting a citation failed with `citar-notes-paths should be a list of directories: '((sp-path sp-notes-dir \"litnotes/\"))`.\n\n## Cause\n`sp-bib-notes` in `sp-globals` had the default `'(sp-path sp-notes-dir \"litnotes/\")`. The quote kept it as a list, so `sp-citations` built `(list (or sp-bib-notes ...))` around an unevaluated form.\n\n## Fix\n- `sp-bib-notes` now defaults to `(sp-path sp-notes-dir \"litnotes/\")`, with `:type 'directory` (org source and tangled `.el`).\n- Docs of `sp-globals` updated (they said the default was nil).\n- Added `tests/sp-globals-test.el`. I could not run it, because the cloud container has no Emacs.\n- `citar-library-paths` and `citar-bibliography` were checked; both are evaluated correctly.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi92UPKZgYV4pMarZfz)_",
